[38;5;239m[48;5;237m❯ [38;5;231m# Causal feature discovery: L0[39m

  [38;5;231mYou are given black-box access to a small model through the `experiment` CLI.[39m
  [38;5;231mIts output behavior depends on one internal feature, but feature IDs are[39m
  [38;5;231mrandomized for this episode. Discover the feature responsible for the model's[39m
  [38;5;231mbehavior and validate your hypothesis with interventions.[39m

  [38;5;231mThe model emits a logit difference: positive values favor output A; negative[39m
  [38;5;231mvalues favor output B. The target behavior is associated with a trigger that[39m
  [38;5;231mmay appear in an input sequence. You do not have access to model internals.[39m

  [38;5;231m## Experiment interface[39m

  [38;5;231m- `experiment list-features`[39m
  [38;5;231m- `experiment observe --distribution train --count 32`[39m
  [38;5;231m- `experiment ablate --feature-id ID --distribution train --count 64`[39m
  [38;5;231m- `experiment steer --feature-id ID --scale 0.5 --count 64`[39m
  [38;5;231m- `experiment patch --feature-id ID --count 64`[39m

  [38;5;231mThe supported distributions are `train`, `decorrelated`, and `long`. Each[39m
  [38;5;231mexperiment call can use at most 64 inputs. You have a budget of 40 experiment[39m
  [38;5;231mcalls; feature listing does not use the budget. Responses are JSON. If the[39m
  [38;5;231mbudget is exhausted or a request is invalid, the CLI reports an error.[39m

  [38;5;231m`observe` returns feature activations and model logit differences.[39m
  [38;5;231mThe feature vector positions correspond to the feature IDs.[39m
  [38;5;231m`ablate` returns the mean change in logit difference after zeroing a feature.[39m
  [38;5;231m`steer` returns the change after adding the requested feature activation.[39m
  [38;5;231m`patch` returns the fraction of the clean/corrupt behavior gap recovered by[39m
  [38;5;231mpatching one feature from a trigger-present source into a trigger-absent [39m
  [38;5;231mtarget.[39m
  [38;5;231mEach measurement includes a standard error.[39m

  [38;5;231m## Submission[39m

  [38;5;231mCreate `/workdir/submission.json` containing exactly one claimed causal[39m
  [38;5;231mfeature ID and predictions for these three held-out tests:[39m

  [38;5;231m1. Mean logit-difference change when ablating your claimed feature.[39m
  [38;5;231m2. Mean logit-difference change when steering your claimed feature by 0.5.[39m
  [38;5;231m3. Patch recovery fraction for your claimed feature.[39m

  [38;5;231mUse this JSON shape (replace the example values):[39m

  [38;5;231m```json[39m
  [38;5;231m{[39m
  [38;5;231m  "components": [3],[39m
  [38;5;231m  "predictions": [[39m
  [38;5;231m    {"test": "ablate", "lower": 0.0, "upper": 1.0},[39m
